{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RaovVNijxWM1N1Hcj7xQop","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t{{ if eq .FailedCheck.Check \"\" -}}\n2\t# Generate Fix Prompt for a Registry Scenario\n3\t\n4\t## Reference Documentation\n5\t{{- range $key, $path := .DocPaths }}\n6\t- Read(`{{ $path }}`) — {{ $key }}\n7\t{{- end }}\n8\t\n9\t## Where the fix goes\n10\t\n11\tWhere the fix template below says, and nowhere else. A model-judged\n12\tscen-check finding is about the words of this one Scenario, its\n13\tdescription or its steps, and is fixed in the Scenario's own entry of\n14\tthe scenario registry; or it is about what a catalogue phrase means,\n15\tand is fixed in that catalogue entry's `means`, in the product\n16\tdocument, where every Scenario using the phrase reads it. The generated\n17\ttest rendered from the Scenario is not edited here: `true-bdd build\n18\ttests --fix` re-renders it from the registry once the entry reads\n19\tcorrectly. A step definition is never edited by a scen-check fix.\n20\t\n21\t## Subject — Registry Scenario\n22\t\n23\t**Scenario ID:** {{.Subject.ID}}\n24\t**Description:** {{.Subject.Description}}\n25\t**Service:** {{.Subject.Service}}\n26\t**Generated test file:** {{.Subject.Path}}\n27\t\n28\t### Steps\n29\t{{.Subject.FormatSteps}}\n30\t### Lineage — user_stories[]\n31\t{{.Subject.FormatUserStories}}\n32\t## Validation Failure\n33\t\n34\tThe following check failed and needs to be fixed:\n35\t\n36\t### Failed Check: {{ .FailedCheck.SectionPath }}\n37\t\n38\t**Question:** {{ .FailedCheck.Question }}\n39\t**Why it matters:** {{ .FailedCheck.Rationale }}\n40\t**Actual:** {{ .FailedCheck.ActualAnswer }}\n41\t\n42\t**Findings** (the reviewer's own lines):\n43\t{{- range .FailedCheck.Context }}\n44\t- {{ . }}\n45\t{{- end }}\n46\t\n47\t**Fix template:**\n48\t{{ .FailedCheck.FixPrompt }}\n49\t\n50\t## Keeping the Scenario in the catalogue's words\n51\t\n52\tWhen the product document declares a `catalogue:` and a Story claims\n53\tthis Scenario (its lineage above is not empty), every step that does\n54\tnot open with `llm:` or `judge:` must match exactly one catalogue\n55\ttemplate, of its own block. A rewritten step stays in an existing\n56\ttemplate's shape: fill the template's slots with new values, or pick\n57\tanother entry whose meaning fits, rather than inventing wording no\n58\ttemplate matches. Read the catalogue before you reword a step. Slots:\n59\t`\"{name}\"` is a quoted run, `{name:number}` digits or `no`,\n60\t`{name:role}` one of the product document's role names, and\n61\t`{name:pattern}` the rest of the step, verbatim.\n62\t\n63\t{{- if .UserAnswers }}\n64\t\n65\t## User Clarifications (from previous questions)\n66\t\n67\tThe user provided the following clarifications:\n68\t{{- range $id, $answer := .UserAnswers }}\n69\t{{- if ne $id \"_user_refinement\" }}\n70\t- **{{ $id }}**: {{ $answer }}\n71\t{{- end }}\n72\t{{- end }}\n73\t\n74\tUse these answers to generate a confident fix. Do not ask these\n75\tquestions again.\n76\t{{- end }}\n77\t\n78\t{{- if index .UserAnswers \"_user_refinement\" }}\n79\t\n80\t## REFINEMENT MODE — User Feedback (CRITICAL)\n81\t\n82\tThe user has reviewed your PREVIOUS fix prompt and is providing\n83\tfeedback to CORRECT IT:\n84\t\n85\t> {{ index .UserAnswers \"_user_refinement\" }}\n86\t\n87\t**CRITICAL INSTRUCTIONS FOR REFINEMENT:**\n88\t1. **DO NOT ask more questions**\n89\t2. **Address the specific issue** — Fix exactly what the user pointed out\n90\t3. **Keep everything else** — Preserve parts of your previous fix that\n91\t   weren't criticized\n92\t4. **Output a fix prompt** — You MUST output FILE_START/FILE_END,\n93\t   NEVER QUESTIONS_START/QUESTIONS_END\n94\t{{- end }}\n95\t\n96\t## Your Task\n97\t\n98\t{{- if index .UserAnswers \"_user_refinement\" }}\n99\t**REFINEMENT MODE**: Apply user feedback and regenerate the fix prompt.\n100\tDO NOT ask questions.\n101\t{{- else if .UserAnswers }}\n102\tUsing the user's clarifications above, generate a complete fix prompt.\n103\t{{- else }}\n104\tDecide whether the Scenario and the documents already say what the\n105\tfixed text must say. When the fix template asks you to ask first and\n106\tthe Scenario leaves the answer open, ask; otherwise generate the fix.\n107\t{{- end }}\n108\t\n109\t**If you can generate a confident fix**, output a fix prompt the applier\n110\tcan execute against the document the fix template names. The fix MUST:\n111\t- Change only what the findings name: the description, the steps they\n112\t  object to, or the `means` of the catalogue entries they name.\n113\t- Keep the behaviour the Scenario specifies. Rewording is the point;\n114\t  re-specifying it silently loses coverage.\n115\t- In the registry, leave the Scenario's id, `service:`, `path:` and\n116\t  `user_stories:` exactly as they are, and every other Scenario too.\n117\t- Give each change as the current text, copied from the subject above,\n118\t  and the exact new text, so the applier replaces rather than composes.\n119\t- Never edit a generated test, a step definition, or a document the fix\n120\t  template does not name.\n121\t\n122\t=== FILE_START: {{.ResultPath}} ===\n123\t# Fix Prompt for Scenario {{.SubjectID}}: {{.Subject.Description}}\n124\t\n125\t## Target\n126\tThe `{{.Subject.ID}}` entry of the `scenarios_yaml` document (the\n127\tscenario registry), or the catalogue entries of the `product` document\n128\tthe findings name.\n129\t\n130\t## Required Changes\n131\t### Change #N: [description]\n132\t**Document:** <scenarios_yaml | product>\n133\t**Field:** <description | merged_steps.<given|when|then> | the means of catalogue entry '<template>'>\n134\t**Current text:**\n135\t```\n136\t<the text as it stands>\n137\t```\n138\t**New text:**\n139\t```\n140\t<the replacement>\n141\t```\n142\t=== FILE_END: {{.ResultPath}} ===\n143\t\n144\t**If you need clarification first**, output questions with suggested\n145\tanswers: each question offers the options